From ef077824f1061225ea784f281a7ca6ecaa7c2fd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:16:16 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 435/437] Navigation: orbit as a turntable by default; Shift
 while orbiting keeps to one direction

Right-drag orbiting used FreeCAD's rounded arcball: moving sideways to look from the side also
tipped the model's vertical axis (feedback 2026-11-26). The default orbit style is now the
turntable (as Tinkercad, Fusion, SketchUp): sideways turns about the vertical axis, up/down tilts,
the model stays upright. Set only when the user has not chosen one.
Holding Shift while orbiting (Tinkercad style) turns only sideways or only up/down, whichever the
mouse moved first; the held position is what is logged, so the spin after release keeps to it.
Checked on a virtual display with xdotool: a 200x160 px diagonal drag with Shift changed only the
azimuth (35.26 deg elevation and no roll kept).
